Apply order 0034 against mariopartyrd/partyboard 98ac07fd1e8f7ab938bbb6fe75789fad99419010 (CC0-1.0; ADR 0009 section 5).
lottery: the COM's crank input stays on its last entry instead of reading past the table, on MPT_PC
Applied in order by runtimes/gc_wii/mp4/CMakeLists.txt with `git apply`.

M4-03, the board sweep (Goomba's Greedy Gala, seed 2, turn 3: a soft lock). In the lottery's ball
game (ExecLottery, game/board/lottery.c) a COM player turns the handle from comInputBall, one
stick position per frame, with comInputPos (a u8) advanced every frame until the handle reaches its
end. The table ends with { 0x7F, 0x7F }, which marks the turn done, but the index ran on past it and
read whatever follows the table in memory: other module data on PC, which differs by layout. On
seed 2 those bytes left the handle still, so the lottery and the turn never ended (the main process
waited in BoardLotteryExec, found from an arena dump of the stuck run). Adding OSReport calls
elsewhere in the module changed the layout and made the hang go away, which is how it showed up as
layout-dependent. The index now stays on the terminator, so the COM's last turn speed is kept and
the handle runs to its end. A COM that finishes within the table, the usual case, is unchanged.
Unconditional on PC.

diff --git a/src/game/board/lottery.c b/src/game/board/lottery.c
index 08ddde0..827f4ce 100755
--- a/src/game/board/lottery.c
+++ b/src/game/board/lottery.c
@@ -868,7 +868,18 @@ static void ExecBallGame(void)
                 spA = HuPadStkY[temp_r25];
             }
             else {
+#ifdef MPT_PC
+                /* The COM's crank input ends at { 0x7F, 0x7F } ("done"), but comInputPos ran on past it
+                 * every frame until the handle reached its end, reading whatever followed the table:
+                 * other module data on PC, which differs by layout and here kept the handle still, so
+                 * the lottery never ended. It stays on the last entry instead. */
+                temp_r23 = comInputBall[comInputPos];
+                if (comInputPos < sizeof(comInputBall) / sizeof(comInputBall[0]) - 1) {
+                    comInputPos++;
+                }
+#else
                 temp_r23 = comInputBall[comInputPos++];
+#endif
                 spB = temp_r23[0];
                 spA = temp_r23[1];
             }
